PHASE 12 — REPOSITORY & CODEBASE ARCHITECTURE

Goal

Create a repository that is organized according to the approved architecture and remains understandable as the system grows.

The repository must not be created as a random collection of files.

The repository structure is an architectural decision.

Core Rule

Repository structure follows architecture, not imagination.

Do not create directories merely because they might someday be useful.

Do not avoid proper boundaries merely because they require slightly more planning.

The repository should contain the minimum structure necessary for the approved architecture while leaving clear, intentional boundaries for future growth.

---

Required Top-Level Structure

At minimum, software projects should use:

project/
├── docs/
├── src/
├── tests/
├── scripts/
├── .github/
├── README.md
├── CHANGELOG.md
├── ROADMAP.md
├── TASKS.md
├── PROJECT_STATE.md
├── CLAUDE.md
├── GEMINI.md
└── ARCHITECT.md

Additional files and directories may be required depending on the technology stack.

---

DOCUMENTATION STRUCTURE

The documentation repository should evolve according to the project.

Example:

docs/
├── idea.md
├── vision.md
├── requirements.md
├── user-stories.md
├── governance.md
├── architecture.md
├── api-contracts.md
